Jean starts with 30 lollipops. She eats 2 lollipops, so she has 30 - 2 = 28 lollipops left.  She wants to package 2 lollipops in one bag.  To find the number of bags she can fill, we divide the number of remaining lollipops by the number of lollipops per bag: 28 / 2 = 14.  So, Jean can fill 14 bags.

